findings.evidence:
Mutants, run in a scratch copy at 8610ebd (Debug, bound max(60 s, 10 x clean)):
- V01: drop the level-rise candidate, so a level-n completion gets no row;
- V02: drop the level clause of `completed`, so the row says not completed, progress 0 and received -before;
- V03: read the cost on NEXT, so a completion row shows the next level's cost;
- V04: drop foreign-exposure credit from AC;
- V05: write AC as the cumulative credit, not the step's;
- V11: the reader reads an empty v6 research array as not recorded.

Each mutant passes ResearchObservationTests 8/8 (about 31 s, bound 322 s) and RunRecordResearchTests 4/4 (about 42 s, bound 436 s).

Second pass with my scratch tests (3/3 pass on clean):
- EveryRepeatableLevelCompletion_HasItsCompletionRow_WithItsLevelAndCost kills V01, V02 and V03 (rig: levels 1000 / 1250 / 1562.5, one per turn);
- ForeignExposureCredit_IsEachStepsCredit_NotTheCumulativeCredit kills V04 and V05 (offered 100 then 300, so paid 100 then 200);
- AV6LineWithAnEmptyResearchArray_ReadsAsRecorded kills V11.

The test files that enable levels or seed exposure (ResearchLevelTests, ResearchOverflowTests, ResearchEurekaCreditTests, DiffusionExposureTests, ResearchExposureControlChangeTests, ResearchSchemaTests) never call the observer or the telemetry writer (grep). The lane's 'independent linear-scan reading' in OnTheProductionWorld re-implements the same formulas (max(before, cost) and the sum of credit deltas), so it checks the implementation, not the definitions.

MEASURED:
- the 850-turn session (seed 42, 1 AI, player researching the cheapest node) has 3,307 node rows and 1,048 completions, all at level 0; its 19 credit rows are each on a different node, so no node is credited twice;
- a 1,280-turn CLI session has 876 completions, all at level 0.

The brief requires 'a completion row on the turn the node completes (turn-exact)'. A level completion is such a completion, and no test covers it.

